A||||8||Boxdin||Why not use block off plates ?||||6||
Z||000000||Boxdin||01-24-2000||06:51 PM||||Egr tubes on V-6s are expensive to replace. Why not eliminate the part and use 2 block off plates. Won't that keep my intake valves cleaner anyway?  My local emmiss wouldn't know the difference. ||||reg||6
Z||000001||TOM||01-24-2000||07:53 PM||||It would probably use more gas and be hard on the catalytic convertor||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||01-24-2000||07:55 PM||||It is actually possible even in California take out the entire EGR system, (Solenoid, valve etc.) and pass smog. Downside, if you have someone who knows what they are doing you might fail the visual. I have not had anybody do it but I have also heard of tests being done directly on the egr to see if its pulling vacuum. You take your chances. It really cleans up the engine area too. Just like taking out the coolant tube that go to the throttle body.||||reg||2
Z||000003||Raydar||01-24-2000||09:26 PM||||The EGR dilutes the fuel mixture so that it will burn a bit cooler. I've heard stories of burned pistons associated with inoperative EGR on the V-6. FWIW...||||reg||1
Z||000004||baggy||01-25-2000||12:26 AM||||can I pull the EGR and smog stuff off of my 2.5??<BR>removing the cat. doesnt bother me..<BR>wont lose a minute of sleep over it..<BR>we dont have inspections down here, yet.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||01-25-2000||01:49 AM||||A friend told me to do that on my 87 4 cyl on a Western Regional trip. On the way home I was asked to get in the back of the line because I was smoking people out! I had no cat so I took care of it by plugging it back in. The 4 cyl EGR tube is nowhere near as big as the V6 so it does not seem to really affect it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||01-25-2000||08:17 AM||||I disconnected my EGR valves vacuum tube and pluged it. its the same basic idea as your block off plate. HOWEVER when i went in for emissions since i forgot that it wasn't hooked up I passed everything EXCEPT Oxides of Nitrogen.  or NOx. The allowable number for here in Georgia is...1374 ppm.  Before it was hooked up it was 21,000 ppm. after hooking it up it changed to 171ppm. this shows that the cumbustion chamber temps are INSANE with out this hooked up. I'll scan these test results and show ya the difference. The car felt like a DOG when i hooked the vacuum tube back to the EGR though.. so about 3 days after the test it came back off. It did effect the mileage. it went up a LOT! went about 125 miles on one tank of gas! (up from usual 90ish) Just make sure that your state doesn't check for the NOx and you can disconnect this valve. Or just take the factory tube to NAPA or local radiator shop and have them dip it in the Radiator dip they have and POOF clean new tube.  You can polish this tube with a little Mothers and a polishing wheel on a dremel! OOOOh shiney! ||||reg||1
Z||000007||mwbackus||01-25-2000||01:36 PM||||Well.. thats the first factual evidence I have heard supporting the claims that the EGR system has an effect on combustion temperature, and it seems to be quite a dramatic effect as well.  Before and after emission scans such as these would indeed be much better data then; "I heard/seen pistons get burned without it" (an event that could easily be caused by various other factors).  <P>I had been considering the use of a chip that disables the EGR system, but somehow compensates by modification of the code.  The Fiero V6 already runs slightly rich with its stock calibrations, so I cannot see how a marked decrease in combustion chamber temperatures could be acheived by altering the fuel map or timing curve.  <P>The reason I was interested in this chip was to eradicate the 1500 rpm deceleration bump down, which I find quite annoying.  Until I obtain more data and a better understanding as to the effects of this new chip, I think I will just use the stock prom. Perhaps I will even buy a NEW egr valve!  Thanks for the info...<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||01-25-2000||02:10 PM||||If you need more info on various chip set contact the guys at Custom Network Motors. turbocnm@aol.com or <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  they can fill you inon anything you might want to know. The 2 lead techs also both hold Physics and one an ME (mechanical engineering)degrees from Ga. Tech. they burned my new chip for me! i passed emissions!  ||||reg||1
